BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:Meetup: TILE Language Party
UID:event_316218202@meetup.com
SEQUENCE:1
DTSTAMP:20260822T021622Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T181500
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260827T203000
SUMMARY:LIMITED SPACE - NEW Korean x English Language Exchange\, Class & B
 oard Games
DESCRIPTION:Toronto's BIGGEST Language Exchange Social Event + Class\n### 
 👨‍🏫 **KOREAN X ENGLISH LANGUAGE EXCHANGE**\n\n* Mini English Class
  with Certified Teacher + Board Games 🎲\n\n### **⚠️ Space is VERY L
 IMITED** so register ASAP to save your spot!\n\n*We can only accept a limi
 ted number of guests due to the venue's space limitations.*\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\
 \-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n\n### **📍 
 LOCATION: CAFÉ PRINCESS**\n\n* 5590 Yonge Street\, North York\n* Across t
 he street from **F**I**NCH SUBWAY STATION**\nnear Shoppers Drug Mart\n\n##
 # *📅* **DATE:** *Thursday\, August 27\, 2026*\n\n* 🕡 Time: 6:15 PM 
 – 8:30 PM\n\n**Please register ASAP** if you want to attend on Aug 27th 
 so we can save your spot!\n\n*We had roughly 80 people sign up for the las
 t event... but we only have space for 30 people max.*\n\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\
 \-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-
 \\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\n**After registering\, please do the following on Aug. 
 27th :**\n\n1. ✅ Do your best to arrive on time @ Café Princess (6:15 P
 M)\n2. ✅ Tell us whether you want to focus on learning/practicing ENGLIS
 H or KOREAN\n3. ✅ Tell us your level: Beginner\, Intermediate\, Advanced
  or Expert\n4. ✅ **Buy 1 item from the Café Princess Menu**\n\n\\-\\-\\
 -\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\\-\
 \-\\-\\-\\-\n**✨ SPECIAL PROMOTION COST: This class is FREE! Simply buy 
 1 item** from the Café Princess menu to participate. Popular menu items i
 nclude:\n\n* *🍓 Strawberry Cheesecake Bingsu*\n* *🍧 Mango or Oreo Bi
 ngsu*\n* *☕ Matcha & Tiramisu Lattes*\n* *🧇 Princess Waffles with Ice
  Cream & Much More*\n\n### **What to Expect**\n\n* *🇰🇷 Guided Korean
  & English language practice*\n* *📚 Interactive mini-lesson led by an a
 ward-winning certified teacher*\n* *🗣️ Structured conversation activi
 ties with native and fluent speakers*\n* *🎲 Board games and social acti
 vities to practice language naturally*\n* *🤝 Make new friends while imp
 roving your communication skills*\n\n### **Learn From an Expert Language T
 eacher**\n\n*John Dias (OCT\, PhD researcher\, MA\, BEd\, HBA & EELC) is a
 n award-winning certified language teacher with 10+ years experience*\n\n#
 ## **Who Should Attend?**\n\n* *English learners (ESL)*\n* *Native Korean 
 speakers wanting to practice English*\n* *Korean learners of all levels*\n
 * *International students\, newcomers\, professionals\, and anyone interes
 ted in language and culture*\n\n**Feel free to e-mail [info@tilelearning.c
 om](mailto:info@tilelearning.com) if you have any questions.**\n**Check ou
 t our [website](https://www.tilelearning.com/) and [instagram](https://www
 .instagram.com/tilelearning/) accounts for more details.**
URL;VALUE=URI:https://www.meetup.com/tilesocial/events/316218202/
